        en: { name: 'Red-Roofed Church, Cap Malheureux', description: 'The little church of Notre-Dame Auxiliatrice with its bright red roof stands on the island’s northernmost cape, against the ocean and the Coin de Mire rock. It is one of the most recognisable postcards of Mauritius.', tip: 'Shoot from the pier by the church at sunset, when the sky glows behind it and Coin de Mire fits into the frame too.' },
